00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:16,000
Cloverfield is a 2008 American found footage monster horror film
directed by Matt Reeves and written by Drew Goddard.

12
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:06,000
It stars Lizzy Caplan, Jessica Lucas, T.J.

13
00:36:50,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Miller (in his film debut), Michael Stahl-David, Mike Vogel, and Odette Yustman.

14
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:46,000
In the film, six friends attempt to flee from a
monster that attacks New York City.

15
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Development began when producer J.

16
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:26,000
Abrams started conceptualizing a monster film and enlisted Neville
Page to design the eventual creature, called Clover.

17
00:48:10,000 --> 00:48:16,000
In February 2007, the project was secretly greenlit by
Paramount Pictures and produced by Abrams's Bad Robot.

18
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Principal photography took place in Los Angeles and New York City in 2007.

19
00:53:50,000 --> 00:53:56,000
The project had several working titles, including Slusho, Cheese, and Greyshot.

20
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
As part of a viral marketing campaign, a teaser trailer was released
ahead of screenings of Transformers (2007) without a title.

21
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:36,000
The final title was revealed in a second teaser trailer
attached to screenings of Beowulf (2007).

22
01:02:20,000 --> 01:02:26,000
With limited pre-release details, it garnered online speculation, including forums and
websites dedicated to uncovering hidden information about the film.

23
01:05:10,000 --> 01:05:16,000
Several tie-ins, including a prequel manga series, were
released as part of the marketing campaign.

24
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Cloverfield was released on January 18, 2008, and received generally positive reviews from
critics, who praised Reeves's direction and the cinéma vérité style narrative.

25
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
It earned $172 million worldwide at the box office against a $25 million budget.

26
01:13:40,000 --> 01:13:46,000
It is the first installment of the Cloverfield franchise, followed by 10
Cloverfield Lane in 2016 and The Cloverfield Paradox in 2018.

27
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
A direct sequel is in development.

28
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
The film explores themes of quarantine, monster,
chaos, skyscraper, supernatural.

29
01:22:10,000 --> 01:22:16,000
The tone is intense and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
